25:["$","section",null,{"id":"$undefined","className":"section-padding bg-muted","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-wide","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center","children":[null,["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] lg:leading-tight","children":"Five questions that usually decide it"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"Work through these in order. By the end, the field is normally down to one or two options."}]]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6","children":[["$","li","Will you have co-owners?",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-lg","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"brand-gradient inline-flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-sm font-bold text-primary-foreground","children":1}],"Will you have co-owners?"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"If you are the only owner, a proprietorship is the only one of the four open to you without bringing someone else in, because a partnership firm, an LLP and a Private Limited Company all require at least two people. A One Person Company exists as a separate route for single founders who want a corporate structure, and is worth asking about if limited liability matters to you but you have no co-founder."}]]}],["$","li","Do you intend to raise outside investment?",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-lg","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"brand-gradient inline-flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-sm font-bold text-primary-foreground","children":2}],"Do you intend to raise outside investment?"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"If yes, a Private Limited Company is effectively the only workable answer. It is the only one of the four that can issue equity shares, create an ESOP pool and take money on a priced or convertible basis. Founders who start as an LLP to save on compliance and then raise funding usually have to pay to convert, which costs more than incorporating correctly at the start."}]]}],["$","li","How much liability does the business carry?",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-lg","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"brand-gradient inline-flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-sm font-bold text-primary-foreground","children":3}],"How much liability does the business carry?"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"This is the question most people underweight. In a proprietorship and a partnership firm, liability is unlimited and personal: business debts reach your own assets. In an LLP and a Private Limited Company it is confined to the entity. If you handle other people's goods or money, hold hazardous material, borrow significantly, or employ people, that difference is real rather than theoretical."}]]}],["$","li","How much annual compliance can you carry?",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-lg","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"brand-gradient inline-flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-sm font-bold text-primary-foreground","children":4}],"How much annual compliance can you carry?"]}],"$L3a"]}],"$L3b"]}]]}]}]
