," →"]}]]}]}],["$","li","partnership-registration",{"children":["$","$L7",null,{"href":"/services/partnership-registration/","className":"hover-lift flex h-full flex-col rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg","children":"Partnership"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"A partnership firm is a business owned by two or more people who have agreed to share its profits, governed by the Indian Partnership Act, 1932. The firm is not a separate legal entity from its partners."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-primary","children":["Explore Partnership Registration"," →"]}]]}]}],["$","li","proprietorship-registration",{"children":["$","$L7",null,{"href":"/services/proprietorship-registration/","className":"hover-lift flex h-full flex-col rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg","children":"Proprietorship"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"A proprietorship is a business owned and run by one individual. It is not a separate legal entity and is not incorporated: in law the proprietor and the business are the same person."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-primary","children":["Explore Proprietorship Registration"," →"]}]]}]}]]}]]}]}]
27:["$","section",null,{"id":"$undefined","className":"section-padding bg-muted","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-wide","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr]","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl","children":"Still not sure?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"Tell us what you are building, who is involved and whether investment is likely. That is usually enough for us to narrow it to one option and explain why."}]]}],["$","$L3c",null,{"defaultRegistrationType":"Not sure yet, help me choose","heading":"Help me choose a structure"}]]}]}]}]
28:["$","section",null,{"id":"$undefined","className":"section-padding","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-wide","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary","children":"FAQs"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] lg:leading-tight","children":"Comparing business structures"}],null]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl divide-y divide-border rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card","children":[["$","details","Which is better, a Private Limited Company or an LLP?",{"className":"group","id":"compare-faq-1","name":"compare-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Which is better, a Private Limited Company or an LLP?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Neither is better in the abstract. A Private Limited Company can issue equity and is what investors expect, but it carries a statutory audit from its first year and more ongoing filing. An LLP has lighter compliance and flexible profit sharing, but cannot raise equity. If funding is in your plan, choose the company; if the business will be owned and run by the same small group, the LLP usually costs less to maintain."}]}]]}],["$","details","Is a partnership firm or an LLP better for two people starting a business?",{"className":"group","id":"compare-faq-2","name":"compare-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Is a partnership firm or an LLP better for two people starting a business?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"An LLP, in most cases, for one reason: liability. In a partnership firm both partners are personally liable without limit, including for each other's acts in the firm's name. In an LLP each partner's liability is capped at their agreed contribution and they are not liable for another partner's wrongful acts. The trade-off is two annual ROC filings that a partnership firm does not have."}]}]]}],["$","details","Can I start as a proprietorship and change later?",{"className":"group","id":"compare-faq-3","name":"compare-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can I start as a proprietorship and change later?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes, and many businesses do. A proprietor can incorporate a company or an LLP and transfer the business into it, or bring in a partner to form a partnership. Conversion is not free: it means new registrations, a new bank account, new GST registration and updating vendor and customer records. That is an argument for thinking it through at the start, not for avoiding a proprietorship if it genuinely fits now."}]}]]}],"$L3d","$L3e"]}]]}]}]
